// NEGATIVE TEST — `..5` has no low end (N6-03).
//
// The mirror of `tests/reject/range_pattern_open_ended.pd`, and a SEPARATE parser
// branch: a missing HIGH end is caught after `..` is consumed, while a missing LOW
// end is caught in primary position, before any range parsing starts. One fixture
// could not cover both, and the branch nobody exercises is the branch that rots.
fn main() {
    let v = match 4 {
        ..5 => 1,
        _ => 0,
    };
    print_int(v);
}
